config AC_FS
	tristate "acfs: the Agent Computer File System"
	depends on BLOCK && PAGE_SIZE_4KB
	select BUFFER_HEAD
	select CRC32
	select XXHASH
	help
	  A copy-on-write file system with branches: a branch is a tree
	  of files that shares its blocks with the branch it was made
	  from until either changes them, so making one is O(1).
	  Mounting a device gives its main branch, or another with
	  -o branch=NAME; ioctls make, list and delete branches and
	  read-only snapshots. AgentOS gives each agent its own branch
	  of a workspace. See Documentation/userspace-api/ac/acfs.rst.

	  If unsure, say N.
